# Files that run inside the Linux container keep LF whatever the checkout does.
#
# A shell script checked out with CRLF has "#!/bin/sh\r" as its shebang, and the
# kernel looks for an interpreter called "/bin/sh\r". The error is "no such file
# or directory" naming a file that plainly exists, which is a bad hour for
# whoever hits it. This repository is developed on Windows, so it would happen.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.toml          text eol=lf
docker-compose.yaml text eol=lf
